CRYPTOGRAPHIC COMPONENTS

The Software uses the following cryptographic primitives:

- SHA-256 for hash chain construction (Python standard library hashlib)
- Ed25519 for digital signatures (PyNaCl — libsodium binding)
- Merkle trees for batch proof exports

These components are used as described in the documentation. Zorynex makes no
warranty regarding their suitability for any particular regulatory requirement.
Users are responsible for validating compliance with applicable regulations in
their jurisdiction, including SR 11-7, the EU AI Act, and CFPB requirements.

